  "notes": "LA live-band R&B — the research calls it \"the most 'played' board in the 2000s lane\", 1999–2010. Tempo is \"56–92: ballads 56–73 half-time (backbeat on 3), mid-tempos 88–92 straight\", and the ballad band is the base with `halfTime` true. The three drum deltas are about feel rather than placement, because that is what the entry claims: \"real-drum snare samples and played ride/hat rather than a rigid 16th grid… plus hand percussion. Their sound is a band recorded, not a loop assembled.\" So `quantizeStrength` falls to 0.54 — the loosest in this section — `velocityVar` is 0.28, `snare.offGridMs` runs 5–11 ms, the hat moves to a played 8th base, and the perc bed is five lanes (ride, conga, tambourine, shaker, bongo) at three to six hits a bar. The identifying harmonic parameter is the mode: \"**modal major** is their signature — 'No Air' is in **F♯ Mixolydian**, which is rare in this lane\", with the sourced cycle `I–VII–ii–IV`. That family carries top weight and `scales` leads with mixolydian, which no other model in this section does. \"Melodies written wide (a 9th–12th range) for power-ballad delivery\" is a thirty-two-semitone melody register with the highest arch weight and a real octave-jump rate. The bass is \"fingered electric bass with legato motion and passing tones; no 808 sub\", so `followRootsProb` 0.5 with a six-wide passing-tone set and walking cells; there is no `bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is medium; the research says the drum detail is \"partly board-level\". ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: \"**F♯ Mixolydian**\" is the entry's own and carries the joint top weight, while the other four values and all five weights are INFERRED from the entry's \"**modal major** is their signature\".",
